{"title":"Career roadmap · Policy Analyst","role":"Policy Analyst","summary":"A Policy Analyst researches public problems, evaluates policies, analyses evidence, studies legislation and regulations, prepares policy briefs, compares policy alternatives and communicates recommendations to governments, think tanks, consulting firms, NGOs, international organisations and corporate public-policy teams.","facts":{},"about":[],"intro":[{"type":"table","header":["Item","Roadmap"],"rows":[[{"text":"Starting point"},{"text":"Year 1 UG · 2026"}],[{"text":"Degree"},{"text":"BA Political Science / BA Honours Political Science"}],[{"text":"Target career"},{"text":"Policy Analyst"}],[{"text":"Career cluster"},{"text":"Humanities & Social Sciences → Public Policy / Governance"}],[{"text":"Core academic areas"},{"text":"Political Science, Public Policy, Governance, Economics, Law"}],[{"text":"Quantitative stack"},{"text":"Statistics, Excel, SQL, Power BI, basic Python"}],[{"text":"Research stack"},{"text":"Research methods, policy evaluation, literature review, data interpretation"}],[{"text":"Communication stack"},{"text":"Policy briefs, reports, presentations, stakeholder communication"}],[{"text":"Strong postgraduate route"},{"text":"MPP / MPA / MA Political Science / Economics / Public Policy"}],[{"text":"Long-term direction"},{"text":"Policy Specialist → Senior Policy Analyst → Policy Lead/Director"}]]}],"horizons":[{"period":"2026–2030","question":"What can I enter now?","output":"Policy research internships, research assistantships, NGO/think-tank roles"},{"period":"2030–2035","question":"How should I specialise?","output":"MPP/MPA/MA + policy research or analyst role"},{"period":"2035–2040","question":"How should I evolve?","output":"Senior Policy Analyst / Policy Specialist / Government Affairs"},{"period":"2040–2046","question":"How can I remain relevant?","output":"Policy leadership, regulatory strategy, policy evaluation and AI governance"}],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A BA in Political Science provides a strong foundation in political institutions, public administration, governance, political theory, international relations and public policy. For competitive policy roles, it should be combined with economics, statistics, research methods, data analysis and policy writing."}]},{"heading":"Career-route check","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["BA Political Science","Policy Research Internship","Research/Policy Assistant","Junior Policy Analyst","Policy Analyst","Senior Policy Analyst","Policy Lead/Manager"]},{"type":"p","text":"A BA can provide a strong foundation, but competitive policy-analysis positions often favour candidates with postgraduate training, research experience, quantitative skills or specialised domain knowledge."}]},{"heading":"What to build each year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["When","Build this","Learn from","Proof of progress","Gap it moves"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1 Sem 1"},{"text":"Political institutions + current affairs"},{"text":"University + government sources"},{"text":"20 policy summaries"},{"text":"Foundations"}],[{"text":"Year 1 Sem 2"},{"text":"Research and academic writing"},{"text":"Research-methods coursework"},{"text":"2 literature reviews"},{"text":"Research"}],[{"text":"Year 2 Sem 1"},{"text":"Public policy + economics"},{"text":"Policy/economics courses"},{"text":"5 policy briefs"},{"text":"Policy reasoning"}],[{"text":"Year 2 Sem 2"},{"text":"Statistics + Excel"},{"text":"NPTEL","url":"https://nptel.ac.in/"},{"text":"Statistical analysis project"},{"text":"Quantitative skills"}],[{"text":"Year 3 Sem 1"},{"text":"Data analysis + policy evaluation"},{"text":"Government datasets + NPTEL"},{"text":"Policy-data project"},{"text":"Evidence-based analysis"}],[{"text":"Year 3 Sem 2"},{"text":"Policy internship"},{"text":"Think tank/NGO/government ecosystem"},{"text":"Internship + policy memo"},{"text":"Professional experience"}],[{"text":"Year 4 Sem 1"},{"text":"Specialisation"},{"text":"Sector-specific research"},{"text":"3 advanced policy briefs"},{"text":"Domain expertise"}],[{"text":"Year 4 Sem 2"},{"text":"Recruitment/PG preparation"},{"text":"MPP/MA/MPA + employer requirements"},{"text":"Portfolio + applications"},{"text":"Career readiness"}]]},{"type":"p","text":"For a 3-year BA, compress the Year 4 activities into the final year."},{"type":"h","text":"Core knowledge stack"},{"type":"h","text":"1. Political Science"},{"type":"p","text":"Build strong understanding of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Indian Constitution"},{"text":"Parliament"},{"text":"Executive"},{"text":"Judiciary"},{"text":"Federalism"},{"text":"Centre–State relations"},{"text":"Local government"},{"text":"Electoral institutions"},{"text":"Political parties"},{"text":"Public administration"},{"text":"Governance"},{"text":"International relations"},{"text":"Comparative politics"},{"text":"Political economy"},{"text":"Public institutions"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Use primary government sources whenever possible."},{"type":"p","text":"Digital Sansad","url":"https://sansad.in/"},{"type":"p","text":"India Code","url":"https://www.indiacode.nic.in/"}]},{"heading":"Public policy","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Learn the complete policy cycle:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Problem identification","Agenda setting","Policy design","Consultation","Implementation","Monitoring","Evaluation","Revision"]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Policy objectives"},{"text":"Stakeholder mapping"},{"text":"Policy instruments"},{"text":"Regulatory approaches"},{"text":"Implementation constraints"},{"text":"Public expenditure"},{"text":"Monitoring"},{"text":"Impact evaluation"},{"text":"Policy trade-offs"},{"text":"Unintended consequences"},{"text":"Evidence-based policymaking"}]}]},{"heading":"Economics","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A strong Policy Analyst needs more economics than a typical BA Political Science curriculum may provide."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Microeconomics"},{"text":"Macroeconomics"},{"text":"Public economics"},{"text":"Fiscal policy"},{"text":"Monetary policy"},{"text":"Inflation"},{"text":"Unemployment"},{"text":"Economic growth"},{"text":"Inequality"},{"text":"Poverty"},{"text":"Externalities"},{"text":"Public goods"},{"text":"Cost-benefit analysis"},{"text":"Labour economics"},{"text":"Development economics"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The goal is not necessarily to become an economist, but to understand the economic consequences of policy decisions."}]},{"heading":"Statistics and research methods","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Build:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Descriptive statistics"},{"text":"Probability fundamentals"},{"text":"Sampling"},{"text":"Correlation"},{"text":"Regression"},{"text":"Hypothesis testing"},{"text":"Confidence intervals"},{"text":"Survey design"},{"text":"Experimental design"},{"text":"Qualitative research"},{"text":"Quantitative research"},{"text":"Mixed methods"},{"text":"Causal inference"},{"text":"Data interpretation"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand the critical distinction:"},{"type":"p","text":"Correlation ≠ causation."},{"type":"p","text":"For policy analysis, learn to ask:"},{"type":"p","text":"What changed, for whom, compared with what alternative, and why?"}]},{"heading":"Data and technology","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Excel"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"XLOOKUP"},{"text":"INDEX/MATCH"},{"text":"IF"},{"text":"SUMIFS/COUNTIFS"},{"text":"Pivot Tables"},{"text":"Charts"},{"text":"Power Query"},{"text":"Data cleaning"},{"text":"Scenario analysis"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Power BI"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Data modelling"},{"text":"Power Query"},{"text":"DAX basics"},{"text":"KPI dashboards"},{"text":"Interactive visualisation"},{"text":"Policy indicators"},{"text":"Geographic visualisation"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Microsoft Power BI","url":"https://www.microsoft.com/power-platform/products/power-bi"},{"type":"h","text":"SQL"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"SELECT"},{"text":"WHERE"},{"text":"GROUP BY"},{"text":"JOIN"},{"text":"CASE"},{"text":"CTEs"},{"text":"Window functions"},{"text":"Aggregation"},{"text":"Date functions"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Python"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn enough to perform:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Data cleaning"},{"text":"Descriptive analysis"},{"text":"Visualisation"},{"text":"Statistical analysis"},{"text":"Basic regression"},{"text":"Reproducible research"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Useful libraries:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"pandas"},{"text":"NumPy"},{"text":"matplotlib"},{"text":"statsmodels"},{"text":"scikit-learn"}]}]},{"heading":"Policy writing","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Policy Analyst must transform research into a decision-ready document."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn to produce:"},{"type":"h","text":"Policy brief"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Executive summary"},{"text":"Problem definition"},{"text":"Evidence"},{"text":"Existing policy"},{"text":"Policy gaps"},{"text":"Options"},{"text":"Advantages/disadvantages"},{"text":"Fiscal implications"},{"text":"Implementation considerations"},{"text":"Recommendation"},{"text":"References"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Other outputs"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Policy memo"},{"text":"Research report"},{"text":"Legislative analysis"},{"text":"Regulatory impact note"},{"text":"Stakeholder brief"},{"text":"Parliamentary research note"},{"text":"Data dashboard"},{"text":"Presentation"},{"text":"Executive summary"}]}]},{"heading":"Government and regulatory research","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Develop the habit of reading primary sources:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Acts"},{"text":"Rules"},{"text":"Regulations"},{"text":"Bills"},{"text":"Parliamentary questions"},{"text":"Government notifications"},{"text":"Budgets"},{"text":"Economic surveys"},{"text":"Committee reports"},{"text":"Annual reports"},{"text":"Official statistics"},{"text":"Consultation papers"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Useful sources include:"},{"type":"p","text":"Press Information Bureau","url":"https://pib.gov.in/"},{"type":"p","text":"NITI Aayog","url":"https://www.niti.gov.in/"},{"type":"p","text":"Ministry of Statistics & Programme Implementation","url":"https://www.mospi.gov.in/"},{"type":"p","text":"Reserve Bank of India","url":"https://www.rbi.org.in/"},{"type":"p","text":"SEBI","url":"https://www.sebi.gov.in/"},{"type":"h","text":"Policy-analysis framework"},{"type":"p","text":"For every policy, practise answering:"},{"type":"p","text":"1. What is the problem?\n2. Who is affected?\n3. How large is the problem?\n4. What caused it?\n5. What is the current policy?\n6. What evidence supports it?\n7. What alternatives exist?\n8. What does each alternative cost?\n9. Who benefits and who bears the cost?\n10. What are the implementation risks?\n11. How will success be measured?\n12. What should policymakers do?"},{"type":"p","text":"This becomes the student's core professional framework."},{"type":"h","text":"Portfolio projects"},{"type":"p","text":"Build at least 8–10 substantial projects."},{"type":"table","header":["Project","What it demonstrates"],"rows":[[{"text":"Education-policy brief"},{"text":"Policy research"}],[{"text":"Healthcare-policy analysis"},{"text":"Sector knowledge"}],[{"text":"Employment-policy study"},{"text":"Economics + policy"}],[{"text":"Urban-policy case study"},{"text":"Governance"}],[{"text":"State-budget analysis"},{"text":"Public finance"}],[{"text":"Election-policy data analysis"},{"text":"Political research"}],[{"text":"Government-scheme evaluation"},{"text":"Policy evaluation"}],[{"text":"Regulatory-impact analysis"},{"text":"Regulatory reasoning"}],[{"text":"Public dataset dashboard"},{"text":"Data skills"}],[{"text":"Comparative policy study"},{"text":"International/comparative analysis"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Capstone"},{"type":"h","text":"\"Evidence-Based Policy Evaluation Dashboard\""},{"type":"p","text":"Choose one government programme and analyse:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Target population"},{"text":"Policy objectives"},{"text":"Budget"},{"text":"Geographic coverage"},{"text":"Beneficiaries"},{"text":"Implementation mechanism"},{"text":"Key indicators"},{"text":"Outcomes"},{"text":"Gaps"},{"text":"Stakeholders"},{"text":"Comparable programmes"},{"text":"Recommendations"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Use official datasets wherever possible."},{"type":"h","text":"Specialisation options"},{"type":"table","header":["Lane","Core stack","Senior direction"],"rows":[[{"text":"Public Policy"},{"text":"Governance + research + data"},{"text":"Senior Policy Analyst"}],[{"text":"Economic Policy"},{"text":"Economics + statistics"},{"text":"Economic Policy Analyst"}],[{"text":"Education Policy"},{"text":"Education + evaluation"},{"text":"Education Policy Specialist"}],[{"text":"Health Policy"},{"text":"Public health + economics"},{"text":"Health Policy Analyst"}],[{"text":"Technology Policy"},{"text":"Technology + regulation"},{"text":"Technology Policy Specialist"}],[{"text":"AI Policy"},{"text":"AI + governance + law"},{"text":"AI Governance Specialist"}],[{"text":"Climate Policy"},{"text":"Climate + economics"},{"text":"Climate Policy Analyst"}],[{"text":"Energy Policy"},{"text":"Energy + regulation"},{"text":"Energy Policy Specialist"}],[{"text":"Financial Policy"},{"text":"Finance + regulation"},{"text":"Financial Policy Analyst"}],[{"text":"International Affairs"},{"text":"IR + geopolitics"},{"text":"International Policy Specialist"}],[{"text":"Trade Policy"},{"text":"Economics + trade"},{"text":"Trade Policy Analyst"}],[{"text":"Urban Policy"},{"text":"Urban governance + data"},{"text":"Urban Policy Specialist"}],[{"text":"Social Policy"},{"text":"Welfare + development"},{"text":"Social Policy Analyst"}],[{"text":"Regulatory Affairs"},{"text":"Law + policy"},{"text":"Regulatory Policy Lead"}],[{"text":"Public Affairs"},{"text":"Policy + stakeholder management"},{"text":"Public Affairs Director"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Four-year honours variant"},{"type":"p","text":"A BA Honours Political Science student should use additional coursework to build:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Public policy"},{"text":"Public administration"},{"text":"Political economy"},{"text":"International relations"},{"text":"Statistics"},{"text":"Economics"},{"text":"Research methodology"},{"text":"Indian Constitution"},{"text":"Comparative government"},{"text":"Governance"},{"text":"Regulatory studies"}]},{"type":"p","text":"An ideal honours profile becomes:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Political Science","Public Policy","Economics","Data","Research","Writing"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"note","label":"Evolve and stay relevant","text":"2035–2046"},{"type":"p","text":"Policy analysis is becoming increasingly data-intensive and technology-driven."},{"type":"p","text":"The future Policy Analyst will need to work with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Administrative datasets"},{"text":"Real-time indicators"},{"text":"Geospatial data"},{"text":"AI-assisted research"},{"text":"Policy simulations"},{"text":"Scenario modelling"},{"text":"Automated literature review"},{"text":"Natural-language interfaces"},{"text":"Digital public infrastructure"},{"text":"AI regulation"},{"text":"Algorithmic accountability"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The human value will increasingly shift toward:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Problem framing","evidence judgement","causal reasoning","ethical judgement","stakeholder understanding","policy design."],"sep":"+"}]},{"heading":"Internships","kind":"internships","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Government / public-sector / research"},{"type":"table","header":["Organisation","Relevant exposure"],"rows":[[{"text":"NITI Aayog"},{"text":"Policy research, development policy"}],[{"text":"Ministry of Statistics & Programme Implementation"},{"text":"Official statistics"}],[{"text":"Parliamentary research ecosystem"},{"text":"Legislative/policy research"}],[{"text":"Ministries of Government of India"},{"text":"Sector-specific policy"}],[{"text":"State Planning Boards/Departments"},{"text":"State policy"}],[{"text":"State Government Departments"},{"text":"Programme implementation"}],[{"text":"RBI"},{"text":"Monetary/financial policy"}],[{"text":"SEBI"},{"text":"Financial regulation"}],[{"text":"Competition Commission of India"},{"text":"Competition policy"}],[{"text":"CAG"},{"text":"Public finance/performance auditing"}],[{"text":"National Health Authority"},{"text":"Health policy"}],[{"text":"Ministry of Environment, Forest & Climate Change"},{"text":"Environmental policy"}],[{"text":"Ministry of Education"},{"text":"Education policy"}],[{"text":"Ministry of Labour & Employment"},{"text":"Labour policy"}],[{"text":"PM Internship Scheme"},{"text":"Broader government/industry experience"}]]},{"type":"p","text":"NITI Aayog","url":"https://www.niti.gov.in/"},{"type":"p","text":"MoSPI","url":"https://www.mospi.gov.in/"},{"type":"p","text":"CAG","url":"https://cag.gov.in/"},{"type":"p","text":"Competition Commission of India","url":"https://www.cci.gov.in/"},{"type":"p","text":"National Health Authority","url":"https://www.nha.gov.in/"},{"type":"h","text":"Think tanks / research organisations"},{"type":"p","text":"Seek internships involving:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Policy research"},{"text":"Data analysis"},{"text":"Legislative research"},{"text":"Public finance"},{"text":"Governance"},{"text":"Development"},{"text":"International affairs"},{"text":"Technology policy"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Examples of organisations to research include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Observer Research Foundation"},{"text":"Centre for Policy Research"},{"text":"Centre for Civil Society"},{"text":"National Institute of Public Finance and Policy"},{"text":"Vidhi Centre for Legal Policy"},{"text":"Indian Council of World Affairs"},{"text":"Institute for Defence Studies and Analyses ecosystem"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Availability changes by organisation and year, so check each organisation's current internship page."},{"type":"h","text":"Private sector"},{"type":"p","text":"Policy Analysts are also hired by:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Public-policy consulting firms"},{"text":"Government-affairs teams"},{"text":"Regulatory consulting firms"},{"text":"Technology companies"},{"text":"Financial institutions"},{"text":"Energy companies"},{"text":"Healthcare companies"},{"text":"Consulting firms"},{"text":"Think tanks"},{"text":"NGOs"},{"text":"International development organisations"},{"text":"Industry associations"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Search titles:"},{"type":"p","text":"Policy Intern · Public Policy Intern · Research Intern · Government Affairs Intern · Regulatory Affairs Intern · Public Affairs Intern · Economic Research Intern · Policy Research Assistant"}]},{"heading":"Certifications in demand","kind":"certifications","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Certification / learning area","Why it matters"],"rows":[[{"text":"NPTEL Public Policy/Political Science"},{"text":"Academic foundation"}],[{"text":"Research Methodology"},{"text":"Research quality"}],[{"text":"Statistics"},{"text":"Evidence analysis"}],[{"text":"Econometrics"},{"text":"Quantitative policy analysis"}],[{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"Data work"}],[{"text":"Power BI"},{"text":"Policy dashboards"}],[{"text":"SQL"},{"text":"Administrative datasets"}],[{"text":"Python"},{"text":"Advanced analysis"}],[{"text":"GIS"},{"text":"Spatial policy analysis"}],[{"text":"Project Management"},{"text":"Policy implementation"}],[{"text":"Monitoring & Evaluation"},{"text":"Programme evaluation"}],[{"text":"Public Finance"},{"text":"Government budgeting"}],[{"text":"Regulatory Impact Assessment"},{"text":"Regulatory policy"}],[{"text":"Data visualisation"},{"text":"Policy communication"}],[{"text":"AI Governance"},{"text":"Future policy work"}]]},{"type":"p","text":"NPTEL","url":"https://nptel.ac.in/"}]},{"heading":"Careers you can be hired as","kind":"careers","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Role","Stack the posting asks for","Where the student proves it"],"rows":[[{"text":"Policy Research Assistant"},{"text":"Research + writing"},{"text":"Policy portfolio"}],[{"text":"Research Associate"},{"text":"Research + analysis"},{"text":"Research project"}],[{"text":"Junior Policy Analyst"},{"text":"Policy + data"},{"text":"Policy brief"}],[{"text":"Policy Analyst"},{"text":"Research + domain expertise"},{"text":"Internship + portfolio"}],[{"text":"Public Policy Associate"},{"text":"Policy + communication"},{"text":"Policy case"}],[{"text":"Government Affairs Analyst"},{"text":"Regulation + stakeholder management"},{"text":"Regulatory project"}],[{"text":"Regulatory Analyst"},{"text":"Regulation + research"},{"text":"Regulatory analysis"}],[{"text":"Public Affairs Associate"},{"text":"Policy + communication"},{"text":"Stakeholder case"}],[{"text":"Legislative Research Assistant"},{"text":"Law + policy"},{"text":"Legislative brief"}],[{"text":"Programme Analyst"},{"text":"Policy + implementation"},{"text":"Programme evaluation"}],[{"text":"Monitoring & Evaluation Associate"},{"text":"Statistics + programme knowledge"},{"text":"M&E project"}],[{"text":"Research Consultant Trainee"},{"text":"Research + presentation"},{"text":"Consulting case"}],[{"text":"Economic Policy Research Assistant"},{"text":"Economics + statistics"},{"text":"Data analysis"}],[{"text":"Development Research Associate"},{"text":"Development + research"},{"text":"Development project"}],[{"text":"ESG/Public Policy Associate"},{"text":"Policy + sustainability"},{"text":"ESG policy project"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Career reality"},{"type":"p","text":"The title Policy Analyst exists across several different sectors, and the entry barrier varies considerably."},{"type":"p","text":"A BA graduate can enter through:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Research Assistant","Policy Associate","Policy Analyst"]},{"type":"p","text":"or:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Government Affairs/Regulatory Intern","Government Affairs Analyst","Policy Analyst"]},{"type":"p","text":"For highly competitive policy institutions, a Master's degree, strong research experience, quantitative capability and excellent writing can significantly strengthen the profile."},{"type":"p","text":"For a student targeting government employment itself, remember:"},{"type":"p","text":"Policy Analyst and Civil Servant are different career routes."},{"type":"p","text":"A Policy Analyst may work with government without being a government civil servant."},{"type":"p","text":"Students who want the civil-service route should separately prepare for UPSC/State PSC or the relevant government recruitment process."}]},{"heading":"Postgraduate study in India","kind":"pg_india","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["PG programme","Best use"],"rows":[[{"text":"Master of Public Policy (MPP)"},{"text":"Direct policy-analysis route"}],[{"text":"Master of Public Administration (MPA)"},{"text":"Government administration"}],[{"text":"MA Political Science"},{"text":"Advanced political analysis"}],[{"text":"MA Public Policy"},{"text":"Policy research"}],[{"text":"MA Economics"},{"text":"Economic policy"}],[{"text":"MA Development Studies"},{"text":"Development policy"}],[{"text":"MA International Relations"},{"text":"Foreign/international policy"}],[{"text":"MA Governance/Public Administration"},{"text":"Government institutions"}],[{"text":"M.Sc Public Policy/Policy Analytics"},{"text":"Quantitative policy"}],[{"text":"MBA Public Policy/Public Affairs"},{"text":"Corporate/government interface"}],[{"text":"MBA Strategy"},{"text":"Policy + business"}],[{"text":"LLM / Law pathway"},{"text":"Regulatory/legal policy, subject to eligibility"}],[{"text":"Master's in Data Science"},{"text":"Data-intensive policy analysis"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Recommended route"},{"type":"p","text":"For a BA Political Science student whose specific goal is Policy Analyst:"},{"type":"flow","items":["BA Political Science","Policy internship","MPP/MPA/MA Public Policy","Research/Analyst role"]},{"type":"p","text":"For a more quantitative profile:"},{"type":"flow","items":["BA Political Science","Economics + Statistics + Data","MPP/Policy Analytics/Economics","Quantitative Policy Analyst"]},{"type":"p","text":"For technology policy:"},{"type":"flow","items":["BA Political Science","Technology + AI + Regulation","MPP/Technology Policy","Tech Policy Analyst"]},{"type":"h","text":"Scholarships and fellowships"},{"type":"p","text":"Potential routes include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"UGC scholarships/fellowships"},{"text":"University research assistantships"},{"text":"PMRF for eligible PhD pathways"},{"text":"Government fellowships"},{"text":"Think-tank research fellowships"},{"text":"International university funding"},{"text":"Fulbright"},{"text":"DAAD"},{"text":"Erasmus+"}]},{"type":"p","text":"UGC","url":"https://www.ugc.gov.in/"},{"type":"p","text":"PMRF","url":"https://www.pmrf.in/"},{"type":"p","text":"USIEF","url":"https://www.usief.org.in/"},{"type":"p","text":"DAAD India","url":"https://www.daad.in/en/"},{"type":"p","text":"Erasmus+","url":"https://erasmus-plus.ec.europa.eu/"},{"type":"p","text":"Eligibility and funding vary by programme."}]},{"heading":"Study abroad, country by country","kind":"abroad","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Country","Example study direction","Scholarship route","Gate to check"],"rows":[[{"text":"USA"},{"text":"Public Policy, Public Administration, Political Economy"},{"text":"Fulbright/university funding"},{"text":"GRE/programme-specific rules"}],[{"text":"UK"},{"text":"Public Policy, International Development, Political Economy"},{"text":"Chevening/university"},{"text":"Academic + English"}],[{"text":"Germany"},{"text":"Public Policy, Governance, Political Science"},{"text":"DAAD"},{"text":"Programme/language"}],[{"text":"France"},{"text":"Public Policy, International Affairs, Governance"},{"text":"Campus France/university"},{"text":"Programme/language"}],[{"text":"Canada"},{"text":"Public Policy, Public Administration, Political Science"},{"text":"University funding"},{"text":"Academic + English"}],[{"text":"Australia"},{"text":"Public Policy, International Development, Governance"},{"text":"University scholarships"},{"text":"Academic + English"}],[{"text":"Netherlands"},{"text":"Public Policy, Governance, Political Science"},{"text":"University scholarships"},{"text":"Programme requirements"}],[{"text":"Singapore"},{"text":"Public Policy, International Affairs"},{"text":"University scholarships"},{"text":"Highly competitive admission"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Application portfolio"},{"type":"p","text":"Prepare:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"BA transcripts"},{"text":"CV"},{"text":"Statement of Purpose"},{"text":"Policy writing sample"},{"text":"Research proposal where required"},{"text":"Academic recommendations"},{"text":"Internship evidence"},{"text":"Quantitative coursework"},{"text":"English test where required"},{"text":"Scholarship essays"},{"text":"Relevant work/research experience"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A policy writing sample can be one of the strongest application assets."}]},{"heading":"Going forward","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career progression"},{"type":"flow","items":["BA Political Science Student","Policy Research Intern","Research Assistant / Policy Associate","Junior Policy Analyst","Policy Analyst","Senior Policy Analyst","Policy Specialist / Policy Lead","Policy Manager / Programme Director","Head of Policy / Public Policy Director"]},{"type":"p","text":"Alternative:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Political Science","Government Affairs","Regulatory Affairs","Public Policy Leadership"]},{"type":"h","text":"PhD routes"},{"type":"p","text":"Potential research areas include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Political Science"},{"text":"Public Policy"},{"text":"Public Administration"},{"text":"Governance"},{"text":"Political Economy"},{"text":"International Relations"},{"text":"Comparative Politics"},{"text":"Development Studies"},{"text":"Public Finance"},{"text":"Education Policy"},{"text":"Health Policy"},{"text":"Technology Policy"},{"text":"AI Governance"},{"text":"Environmental Policy"},{"text":"Climate Policy"},{"text":"Urban Governance"},{"text":"Social Policy"},{"text":"Regulatory Policy"},{"text":"Security Studies"},{"text":"Digital Governance"}]},{"type":"note","label":"2040–2046","text":"Future evolution"},{"type":"p","text":"The strongest Policy Analysts of the future will combine domain expertise with data and technology."},{"type":"p","text":"The progression will increasingly look like:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Policy Research","Evidence Analysis","Policy Evaluation","Scenario Modelling","Policy Design","Strategic Policy Leadership"]},{"type":"p","text":"Emerging areas include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"AI governance"},{"text":"Digital public infrastructure"},{"text":"Data governance"},{"text":"Algorithmic accountability"},{"text":"Cyber policy"},{"text":"Climate policy"},{"text":"Energy transition"},{"text":"Digital competition policy"},{"text":"Platform regulation"},{"text":"Privacy regulation"},{"text":"Technology diplomacy"},{"text":"AI safety policy"},{"text":"Public-sector digital transformation"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The most valuable profile will therefore be:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Political Science","Economics","Data","Research","Policy Writing","Technology","AI"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Best profile to build"},{"type":"p","text":"A high-value undergraduate profile would be:"},{"type":"h","text":"BA Political Science"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Public Policy knowledge"},{"text":"Economics"},{"text":"Statistics"},{"text":"Research Methodology"}]},{"type":"flow","items":["Excel","Power BI","SQL"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Policy Writing"},{"text":"Government-data analysis"},{"text":"Policy internship"},{"text":"One sector specialisation"},{"text":"AI literacy"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Best sector specialisations"},{"type":"p","text":"Choose one by Year 3:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Technology/AI"},{"text":"Healthcare"},{"text":"Education"},{"text":"Climate"},{"text":"Energy"},{"text":"Finance"},{"text":"Agriculture"},{"text":"Urban development"},{"text":"International relations"},{"text":"Defence/security"},{"text":"Labour/employment"},{"text":"Social welfare"},{"text":"Digital governance"}]},{"type":"p","text":"This is stronger than graduating as a generalist with only broad political knowledge."}]}]}